      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s28h",
          "text": "What Is Colorado’s Shared Fault Law?",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b28k",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s28j",
          "text": "Colorado’s shared fault law allows you to recover compensation after hitting an illegally parked car, as long as your responsibility remains below 50 percent, although any recovery will be reduced based on your share of fault. This rule, known as modified comparative negligence, determines how compensation gets adjusted when both parties contribute to a car accident.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b28p",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l28m",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://law.justia.com/codes/colorado/title-13/damages-and-limitations-on-actions/article-21/part-1/section-13-21-111/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s28l",
          "text": "As mentioned in the",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s28n",
          "text": " Colorado Revised Statutes 13-21-111",
          "marks": [
            "l28m"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s28o",
          "text": ", a person may recover damages for injury or property loss when their negligence does not exceed the other party’s, although any award decreases in proportion to their percentage of responsibility.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b28r",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s28q",
          "text": "In practice, a driver who strikes an illegally parked vehicle may still recover compensation when the parked car created a hazard, although any recovery reflects each party’s contribution. These percentages often become the focus of negotiation, especially when factors such as lighting conditions, road layout, and driver behavior influence how responsibility is divided.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b28t",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
